/// Sound effects are currently no-ops. This project originally played
/// flap/point/crash sounds via the `audioplayers` package, but a newer
/// release of that package pulled in Dart's native-assets/`objective_c`
/// bindings, which have an unresolved bug that crashes Windows builds
/// whenever any part of the file path contains a space (a very common
/// situation — see https://github.com/dart-lang/native/pull/3378).
///
/// Every call site elsewhere in this file (playFlap/playPoint/playCrash/
/// setVolume/setMuted/dispose) is unchanged — only this class's internals
/// were gutted — so nothing else needed to be edited. Haptic feedback
/// (HapticFeedback.*, called alongside these at every call site) still
/// provides tactile feedback in the meantime.
///
/// To restore real sound once that upstream bug is fixed: add
/// `audioplayers` back to pubspec.yaml (pin an EXACT version, not a `^`
/// range, and re-check after every `flutter pub get` that `objective_c`
/// hasn't reappeared), add real audio files under `assets/sounds/` and
/// declare them in pubspec.yaml, then reintroduce `AudioPlayer` instances
/// and real playback calls in the methods below.
class SoundManager {
  double _volume = 0.8;
  bool _muted = false;

  void setVolume(double v) {
    _volume = v.clamp(0.0, 1.0);
  }

  void setMuted(bool m) {
    _muted = m;
  }

  Future<void> playFlap() async {}
  Future<void> playPoint() async {}
  Future<void> playCrash() async {}

  void dispose() {}
}

